ey make life more difficult than it has to be. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Another excellent article on the real issues facing us today.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/1518536671827094841/comments/default/3220017419775170629'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/1518536671827094841/comments/default/3220017419775170629'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2010/03/grand-distractions.html?showComment=1267789712907#c3220017419775170629' title=''/><author><name>Luke Fisher</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/06652043844204991418</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='24' src='http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_23Rn4NaHcwc/SeZ8MtqwrLI/AAAAAAAAAAM/UBY05A8mfDI/S220/me+and+mines.jpg'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2010/03/grand-distractions.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-1518536671827094841' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/1518536671827094841' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1964777032"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="March 5, 2010 at 4:48 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-822089782533002800</id><published>2010-03-04T21:04:29.465-07:00</published><updated>2010-03-04T21:04:29.465-07:00</updated><title type='text'>It has been said that Goldman Sachs Rules the Worl...</title><content type='html'>It has been said that Goldman Sachs Rules the World.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Government bureaucrats witlessly do the bidding of entities like Goldman Sachs.  They are witless.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;What&amp;#39;s really curious is the relationship between The Nature Conservancy, Goldman Sachs, the &amp;#39;Endangered Species&amp;#39; Act, and the Federal tax feeders.  There appears to be a direct connection to the CO2/Climate Change Hoax in all this confusion, as well.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.freeenterpriseactionfund.com/GoldmanSachs_shareholder_letter_3-21-06.pdf&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;GS/Paulson/THCConflict&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.rangemagazine.com/pdf/spr03_landlord.pdf&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;NatureConservancy/Conflict&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;It&amp;#39;s so darned complicated!&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;And now,  all that fallow land in South America &amp;amp; here-and-there across this planet can be purchased by the major industrial polluters for CO2 &amp;#39;tokens&amp;#39; so they can continue blowing smoke unmolested.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;The rest of us will need to give up our cars, wood burning stoves, air conditioners, old people, and belching sheep.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/1518536671827094841/comments/default/822089782533002800'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/1518536671827094841/comments/default/822089782533002800'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2010/03/grand-distractions.html?showComment=1267761869465#c822089782533002800' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2010/03/grand-distractions.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-1518536671827094841' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/1518536671827094841' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1671018176